\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qc\cf1\b\fs28\lang12 Wampserver - HTTPS SSL in "manual" mode\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\fs24 - 1 - Where are the "manual" HTTPS SSL tools?\par
- 2 - Prerequisites for creating CA and SSL certificates\par
- 3 - Creating self-signed certificate.\par
- 4 - Creating certificate and private key for a domain\par
- 5 - Tell Apache that the VirtualHost my-domain.internal is in HTTPS SSL mode\par
\cf0\b0\fs22 Since version 3.3.2, Wampserver has included the tools needed to support https SSL automatically.\par
From version 3.2.6.4 onwards, Tray Menu Manager integrates tools for generating self-signed certificates and private keys to support https SSL manually.\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1 These "manual" tools are compatible with Wampserver's automatic https SSL mode.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\cf1\b\fs24 - 1 - Where are the "manual" HTTPS SSL tools?\par
\cf0\b0\fs22 "Self Signed" tab in About Tray Menu Manager\par
So, double-click on the Wampmanager icon or right-click -> About... then select the "Self Signed" tab.\par
This "Self Signed" tab itself comprises four tabs:\par
- \b 1.1 \b0 - Certificate Domain Name (CDN)\par

\pard\li720\sl240\slmult1 -- Certificate Domain Common Name\par
Designation of self-signed certificate name (e.g. Wampserver Certificate No. 1) or domain name (e.g. domain.internal) for certificates and private domain keys.\par
-- Private Key File Password\par
Mandatory password to remember.\par
-- Local Server IPv4 or IPv6\par
To be left on 127.0.0.1 (except for experts).\par
-- SAN Certificate (Subjet Alternate Names)\par
When creating private keys domain.tld, may contain other domain names.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1 - \b 1.2\b0 - Properties and Certificate Authority (PCA)\par

\pard\li720\sl240\slmult1 Self-signed certificate credentials and properties.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1 - \b 1.3 \b0 - Create and Save New Certicate (CSNC)\par

\pard\li720\sl240\slmult1 Several roles:\par
- Create self-signed certificate (Create CA Cert)\par
- Load previously created self-signed certificate (Load CA Cert)\par
- Create domain SSL certificate (Create SSL Cert)\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1 - \b 1.4\b0  - Verify Log\par

\pard\li720\sl240\slmult1 View log\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\cf1\b\fs24 - 2 - Prerequisites for creating CA and SSL certificates in manual mode\par
\cf2\ul\fs26 If Wampserver's automatic HTTPS SSL mode is already enabled, i.e. if :\par
\ulnone\tab\i Right-click -> Wamp settings -> Wampserver ready to support https\par
\ul\i0 is checked, go directly to point - 3 -\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\ulnone This item may be checked, as the manual HTTPS SSL mode is compatible with the automatic HTTPS SSL mode.\ul\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs22 - \b 2.1 \b0 - To ensure compatibility with Wampserver's automatic HTTPS SSL mode.\par
The contents of the file: \par
C:\\wamp64\\bin\\apache\\apache2.4.xx\\conf\\extra\\httpd-ssl.conf must be replaced by :\par
_____ Beginning of file (not included) _____\par
\f1 #\par
# This is the Apache server configuration file providing SSL support.\par
# When we also provide SSL we have to listen to the\par
# standard HTTP port and to the HTTPS port\par
#\par
Listen 0.0.0.0:443 https\par
Listen [::0]:443 https\par
\par
# Where the certificates are\par
Define CERTIFS $\{INSTALL_DIR\}/bin/Certs\par
Define CERTIFICATS $\{INSTALL_DIR\}/bin/certificats\par
\par
Protocols h2 h2c http/1.1\par
<IfModule mod_headers.c>\par
  Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; preload"\par
</IfModule>\par
SSLSessionCache shmcb:$\{INSTALL_DIR\}/tmp/ssl_gcache_data(512000)\par
SSLOptions +StrictRequire +StdEnvVars -ExportCertData\par
# SSL Protocol support:\par
SSLProtocol -all +TLSv1.2 +TLSv1.3\par
SSLCompression Off\par
SSLHonorCipherOrder On\par
# SSL Cipher Suite:\par
SSLCipherSuite SSL ECDHE-ECDSA-CHACHA20-POLY1305:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-CHACHA20-POLY1305:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384\par
# Encryptions TLSv1.3\par
SSLCipherSuite TLSv1.3 TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256:TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384\par
SSLOpenSSLConfCmd ECDHParameters secp521r1\par
SSLOpenSSLConfCmd Curves sect571r1:sect571k1:secp521r1:sect409k1:sect409r1:secp384r1\par
\par
## Never modify these four lines\par
## BEGIN OF SSL VIRTUAL HOST CONTEXT\par
## END OF SSL VIRTUAL HOST CONTEXT\par
## To be repeated for another SSL VirtualHost\par
\par
# Do not remove these lines UnDefine\par
UnDefine SERVERNAMEVHOSTSSL\par
UnDefine DOCUMENTROOTVHOSTSSL\par
\f0 _____ End of file (not included) _____\par
\par
Don't forget to save the modified file.\par
\par
- \b 2.2 \b0 - In the file C:\\wamp64\\bin\\apache\\apache2.4.xx\\conf\\httpd.conf\par
- 2.2.1 - Replace\par
\f1 #LoadModule socache_shmcb_module modules/mod_socache_shmcb.so\par
\f0 with\par
\f1 LoadModule socache_shmcb_module modules/mod_socache_shmcb.so\par
\f0 - 2.2.2 - Replace\par
\f1 #LoadModule ssl_module modules/mod_ssl.so\par
\f0 with\par
\f1 LoadModule ssl_module modules/mod_ssl.so\par
\f0 - 2.2.3 - Replace\par
\f1 #Include conf/extra/httpd-ssl.conf\par
\f0 with\par
\f1 Include conf/extra/httpd-ssl.conf\par
\f0\par
Don't forget to save the modified file.\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs24 - 3 - Creating self-signed certificate.\par
\cf0\b0\fs22 - \b 3.1 \b0 - Self-signed certificate credentials and properties.\par
Go to the "Properties and Certificate Authority" tab (see 1.2 above) and fill in the various fields below:\par
-- \i Country Code\i0 : \tab\tab the two-letter country code, e.g. 'FR' for France\par
-- \i Organization Name \i0 : \tab Whatever you want, for example 'Otomatic & Co'.\par
-- \i Organizational Unit \i0 : \tab Whatever you like, e.g. 'engineering\par
-- \i Address \i0 : \tab\tab\tab I put the postal code and the name of the district: '75017 - Epinettes'.\par
-- \i Locality\i0 : \tab\tab\tab Your city, for example 'Paris'.\par
-- \i State/County \i0 : \tab\tab Your country or state, for example 'France'.\par
-- \i Email \i0 : \tab\tab\tab May be an invalid address: toto@toto.invalid\par
-- \i Cert Period days \i0 :\tab\tab  Certificate validity period in days, 999 maximum\par
\par
All this information is memorized and you won't have to enter it again, unless you want to modify it.\par
- \b 3.2 \b0 - Creating a self-signed certificate\par
- 3.2.1 - Go to the "Certificate Domain Name" tab (See 1.1 above)\par
Fill in the 'Certificate Domain Common Name' field with the name you want to give to the self-signed certificate, for example: '\i Wampserver Cert No 1\i0 '.\par
Fill in the 'Private Key File Password' field with the password of your choice. Make a note of this password, which will be used later.\par
- 3.2.2 - Go to the "Create and Save New Certificate" tab (see 1.3 above)\par
Validate the [Create CA Cert] button\par
A popup displays "Finished collecting and saving certificate for Wampserver Cert No 1"\par
Validate OK of the popup.\par
If you validate the "Verify log" tab, you'll see the log of the entire self-signed certificate creation process, which can be found in: C:\\wamp64\\bin\\certificats\\Wampserver_Cert_No_1.pfx\par
A single self-signed certificate is all you need to create multiple certificates and domain private keys.\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs24 - 4 - Creating a certificate and private key for a domain\par
\cf0\b0\fs22 - \b 4.1 \b0 - Go to the "Certificate Domain Name" tab (see 1.1 above)\par
Validate the [Clear Domains] button\par
Fill in the "Certificate Domain Common Name" field with the name of the local domain you wish to switch to HTTPS SSL mode, e.g. 'my-domain.internal'.\par
Fill in the 'Private Key File Password' field with the password you've written down.\par
- \b 4.2 \b0 - Go to the "Create and Save New Certificate" tab (see 1.3 above)\par
Using the Tree button in the CA Certificate field, open the self-signed certificate created in 3.2.2, in our case :\par
C:\\wamp64\\bin\\certificats\\Wampserver_Cert_No_1.pfx\par
Fill in the 'CA Private Key Password' field with the password you've written down.\par
Validate the [Load CA Cert] button\par
Validate the [Create SSL Cert] button\par
A popup displays "SSL certificate created successfully".\par
Validate OK of the popup\par
If you validate the "Verify log" tab, you'll see the logs of the entire certificate and private key creation process for the domain, which in the end can be found in :\par
C:\\wamp64\\bin\\certificats\\my-domain.internal-certonly.pem\par
C:\\wamp64\\bin\\certificats\\my-domain.internal-privatekey.pem\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs24 - 5 - Tell Apache that the VirtualHost my-domain.internal is in HTTPS SSL mode\par
\cf0\b0\fs22 - \b 5.1\b0  - Insert the following text in the C:\\wamp64\\bin\\apache2.4.xx\\conf\\extra\\httpd-ssl.conf file just before the line:\par
\f1 ## Never modify these four lines\par
\ul\f0 To remain compatible with Wampserver's VirtualHost management, \cf3 the domain-name.tld, in this case 'my-domain.internal', is written three times: \cf0 start and end comments (##) and the Define SERVERNAMEVHOSTSSL line.\par
\ulnone The VirtualHost folder (Define DOCUMENTROOTVHOSTSSL) is the same as in\par
C:\\wamp64\\bin\\apache2.4.xx\\conf\\extra\\httpd-vhosts.conf\par
and must not include a trailing slash.\par
______ Start of text (Not included) _____\par
\par
\f1 ## BEGIN OF SSL VIRTUAL HOST my-domain.internal CONTEXT\par
Define SERVERNAMEVHOSTSSL my-domain.internal\par
Define DOCUMENTROOTVHOSTSSL G:/www/aviatechno\par
<VirtualHost *:443>\par
  ServerName $\{SERVERNAMEVHOSTSSL\}\par
  DocumentRoot "$\{DOCUMENTROOTVHOSTSSL\}"\par
  SSLEngine on\par
  SSLCertificateFile      "$\{CERTIFICATS\}/$\{SERVERNAMEVHOSTSSL\}-certonly.pem"\par
  SSLCertificateKeyFile   "$\{CERTIFICATS\}/$\{SERVERNAMEVHOSTSSL\}-privatekey.pem"\par
  <Directory "$\{DOCUMENTROOTVHOSTSSL\}/">\par
    Options +Indexes +Includes +FollowSymLinks +MultiViews\par
    AllowOverride all\par
    Require local\par
  </Directory>\par
  CustomLog "$\{INSTALL_DIR\}/logs/custom.log" "%t %h %\{SSL_PROTOCOL\}x %\{SSL_CIPHER\}x \\"%r\\" %b"\par
</VirtualHost>\par
## END OF SSL VIRTUAL HOST my-domain.internal CONTEXT\par
\par
\f0 _____ Fin du texte (non inclus) _____\par
\par
Don't forget to save the modified file.\par
\par
- \b 5.2\b0  - Right-click -> Restart from scratch\par
VirtualHost my-domain.internal should be in HTTPS SSL mode.\par
\par
}
